## The unit and the law
- THE UNIT IS THE POOL (a wording set = one pool's k existing variants, each rewritten in place under the SAME `vid`, each given a `[plain]` line and three `[face]` sub-rows in the ARCH §2.5 grammar); NO variant is added or removed (NEVER TRIM; the variant ratchet and the face-count ratchet of 8a red on any fall); the typed lines of the pool are NOT touched (ROLE · READS · RELATION · ATTACH · FORM · MOVE); a row's `[grammar: Vn]` and slots are the card's.
- EVERY writer, refiner and refuter reads the VOICE documents whole (the list is the taste workflow's `VOICE` string: REGISTER-CARD with S2 + S3; Part B §1, §16–§16.2, §18, §20–§23; MOVE-GRAMMAR §1–§3, §4.4.1–§4.4.3; CLERK-LAWS §2.4.1, §2.6.1; ARCH §2.5 + §8.3) and the pool's LICENCE CARD printed from the census in the dock (`node scripts/prose-licence-card.mjs <block> '<pool>'`), and the block's own annex section for the spines beside it.
- THE GATE is 8a's `scripts/prose-wave-gate.mjs` (read its header for the usage line before writing a prompt that calls it; the flags are the taste harness's `--arm draft --round N` / `--arm A --base <cells.json>` unless the header says otherwise): the projector `generate-dossier-state-prose.mjs --check` must accept every row or name the refusal; the composed walker at N (owned grain; the spine's inherited findings listed, never charged); the classifier over the DRIFT run against the block's base cells — every cell of the block WORDING-ONLY (or RE-INDEXED under the index-stable draw, printed and counted), nothing REPLACED, no STOP; the band figures at BOTH grains (8a item 5a); sibling swaps 0 and the distance figure; provenance ≤ 1 per unit on a licensed holder; the duplicate-unit rate on VARIETY for the block before and after; the round counters per pool.
- PHASE 1 (the draft, Opus): one Opus writer per pool per round; rounds continue while a failing OWNED measure moves; two consecutive dry rounds → the pool is a REFUSAL row (banked, never trimmed; its last packet kept); hard cap 6 rounds logged. PHASE 2 (the refinement, Opus, a DIFFERENT agent than the drafter): every pool refined ONCE toward the CEILING (Part B §21.1–§21.4: the sharpest licensed fact, the strongest rhythm inside the voice, the four faces as far apart as the voice allows, zero tics, the clerk's ear; the density law; never plainer with no law behind it); the gate re-runs; the keep-or-revert rule per pool (lawful stays lawful → keep; unlawful with failures fallen and none new → keep; else revert from `git show <draft>:annex`). PHASE 3 (the refute, FABLE, EVERY pool, never a sample): one Fable refuter per pool over the kept rows, blind to nothing (there is one arm now), with the refuters' grounds of SITTING §T.5 named in the prompt (tails as qualifications; sibling paraphrase; forecast or perfect aspect on a standing fact; a claim opened by an ambiguity after the spine; a restatement; costume in the syntax; a positive share on a gated `< 1`; a same-page contradiction; an unlicensed particular; a citation with no licensed source; a regression against the draft on a named target); default FAIL when uncertain; each finding names its LAW. PHASE 4 (the judgment, FABLE): one Fable JUDGE per block applies the chair's rules per VARIANT — a FAIL that names a law and quotes the face → that face REVERTS to its draft face (one for one; the variant keeps its other faces); a WITHHELD → keep, listed; a FAIL naming no law → WITHHELD; a face reverted to a draft face that the refuter also failed → the pool is a REFUSAL row for the chair; the judge writes `rewrite/<block>/JUDGMENT.md` with every ruling and its ground, and commits the resulting annex + regenerated leaves in the block's dock as `REWRITE 8b <block>: <kept variants>/<n> · <reverted faces> · <refusals>`. The chair reads every JUDGMENT.md (a sample re-derived by hand) at the block's fold.
- SHIFT 1 IS DECLARED PER BLOCK on the classifier's print (WORDING-ONLY per cell; RE-INDEXED where the index-stable draw moved a pick; the counts into the block's receipt and the shift register's declared row) — signed by the chair under the delegation of §T.12, vetoable, and the manifest fixture is re-recorded ONCE at the REWRITE's last car (the freeze act), never per block.
- FENCES for every agent: writers, refiners and refuters write ONLY their packet under `$SC/rewrite/<block>/<pool dir>/`; they never enter, edit, commit or run tests in any dock; they may READ the dock and run the read-only licence-card script there. The gate and the judge work ONLY in the block's dock; explicit staging; never stash/amend/rebase/checkout/reset --hard; no register `--write` beyond the lighting census by its own ritual (the corpus-pinning walkers RED in a never-landed dock are DECLARED for the block, never re-frozen there — the landing consist re-freezes them once, at the chair's register car); the runner count in its own shell before every vitest.
- COST AND CLOCK are measured per phase per block from the workflow's budget counter and printed in the block's receipt (the owner's row 26 is a report; the numbers keep flowing).

